   "html": "<h1><span class=\"kind\">class</span> ara::com::SamplePtr</h1>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<p class=\"meta\"><span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CM_00306\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">[SWS_CM_00306]</a></span> <span class=\"ups\">Upstream: <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00202\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00202</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00203\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00203</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf#nameddest=RS_AP_00114\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf)\">RS_AP_00114</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf#nameddest=RS_AP_00122\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf)\">RS_AP_00122</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf#nameddest=RS_AP_00135\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf)\">RS_AP_00135</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf#nameddest=RS_AP_00145\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf)\">RS_AP_00145</a></span></p>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\" id=\"class-decl\">template &lt;typename T&gt; class SamplePtr {...};</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Emulates a std::unique_ptr to an event sample.</p><p>The <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_com_SamplePtr_f95130.html\">ara::com::SamplePtr</a> behaves as a std::unique_ptr as long as the event/ field is subscribed to, or the Proxy it belongs to is not destroyed. The precondition defined in <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CM_00085\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">[SWS_CM_00085]</a> and <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CM_00087\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">[SWS_CM_00087]</a> must be fulfilled. Otherwise it is considered a violation.</p><p>Note: The SamplePtr is always passed with a const SampleType to the callable in GetNewSamples() (see <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CM_00701\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">[SWS_CM_00701]</a>). Therefore the sample datatype (typename T) and the SamplePtr operators using the sample datatype (typename T) are implicitly declared as const. This means that the sample data will always be read-only.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
